Lobium native fingerprint hooks — hardwareConcurrency override + config channel read.

COMPILE-VERIFIED against Chromium 152.0.7928.0 (built on a 12-core machine, ~6.5h stock + ~2min
incremental). This is the FULL current state of the proven build tree, captured so `lobium/` alone
reconstructs the fork from a clean Chromium fetch (see lobium/REPRODUCIBLE_BUILD.md).

Two capabilities, one diff over two files:

  (A) PROVEN end-to-end — the single-value switch `--lobium-hwc=<n>`:
      navigator.hardwareConcurrency reports <n> instead of the host CPU count, computed in C++ inside
      Blink, so there is NO JS-detectable tell (the exact thing the interim patchright/CDP engine
      cannot do). Proven live: baseline HWC=12 -> --lobium-hwc=99 => HWC=99 -> --lobium-hwc=4 => HWC=4.

  (B) COMPILES, file-read LIMITED — the production config channel `--lobium-fp-config=<lobium-fp.json>`:
      the switch is forwarded to the renderer and the getter parses the JSON (base::JSONReader::ReadDict
      -> navigator.hardwareConcurrency). The reader compiles and links, but this getter runs in the
      RENDERER process, whose sandbox denies arbitrary file reads — so base::ReadFileToString fails and
      it falls back to the host value. The production design must read lobium-fp.json in the BROWSER
      process (unsandboxed) and plumb resolved values to the renderer via switches/mojo, OR have the
      sidecar resolve the file and pass scalars like --lobium-hwc directly. Tracked as the next Lobium
      step; the config schema + writer already exist (lobium/config-channel.md, lobium/src/
      lobium_fp_config.{h,cc}, engine-runner lobium-config.ts). The same hook shape extends to the deep
      surfaces (canvas/WebGL/audio) that ONLY native patching can spoof coherently.

Two hooks:
  1. content/browser/.../render_process_host_impl.cc — forward --lobium-hwc + --lobium-fp-config to the
     renderer command line.
  2. third_party/blink/.../navigator_concurrent_hardware.cc — the getter resolves the override once
     (cached), preferring the config file then the single-value switch.

